{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.QbetaC4FromC3C8ProductIdentity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.QbetaC4FromC3C8ProductIdentity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.c4_via_quotient_at_silver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.c4_via_quotient_at_silver","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qbeta-c4-from-c3-c8-product-identity.lean#L56-L61","doc":"**The derivation chain: c_4 = c_8 / c_3 at silver.**\n\nCombines `c4_eq_c8_div_c3_at_silver` into the explicit quotient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.c4_at_silver_eq_neg_49_32","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.c4_at_silver_eq_neg_49_32","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qbeta-c4-from-c3-c8-product-identity.lean#L47-L54","doc":"**c_4 closed form at the silver ratio.**\n\nc_4 := -2 · b⁴ = -2 · (7/8)² = -49/32, where b² = 7/8 at silver.\nThis is the structural closed form `c_4 = -2·b⁴`, consistent with\n`c_4 = c_8 / c_3` proved above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.c3_times_c6_eq_c9_at_silver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.c3_times_c6_eq_c9_at_silver","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qbeta-c4-from-c3-c8-product-identity.lean#L39-L45","doc":"**Independent structural check: c_3 · c_6 = c_9 at silver.**\n\nVerifies the companion product identity at silver: c_3 = -2,\nc_6 = 7/2, c_9 = -7. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.c4_eq_c8_div_c3_at_silver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.c4_eq_c8_div_c3_at_silver","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qbeta-c4-from-c3-c8-product-identity.lean#L30-L37","doc":"**c_4 from c_3 · c_8 (at silver).**\n\nVerifies `c_3 · c_4 = c_8` at the silver ratio b² = 7/8,\nwhere c_3 = -2, c_4 = -49/32, c_8 = 49/16. Equivalently\n`c_4 = c_8 / c_3 = -49/32`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:qbeta-c4-from-c3-c8-product-identity","label":"prop:qbeta-c4-from-c3-c8-product-identity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qbeta-c4-from-c3-c8-product-identity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}